id=a52sxq_apex_dm_relabel
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: no reboot after a flash when a Play-updated APEX loses its label
author=kusti420
description=Diagnosed 2026-10-22 (K8, tester report "Mountify bootloop"): on this 5.4 kernel the dm "add" uevent comes before the device is in the dm hash, so ueventd sometimes cannot look up the name of a new APEX dm device (ueventd: Failed to find device dev: 253:58) and relabels /dev/block/dm-N from apex_dm_device to dm_device. system_server is then denied reading it (avc getattr dm_device), PackageManager cannot parse that Play-updated APEX (com.android.scheduling, first data APEX = dm-58) and Samsung's InstallPackageHelper.tryToRecover reboots (reboot,recoverydecompressedapex). It only matters when PackageManager re-parses APEXes (after a flash or a cleared package cache), about 1 boot in 6 on the test phone, sometimes twice in a row; KernelSU metamodules such as Mountify count that as a bootloop and disable themselves. Fix: at post-fs-data, after apexd has activated everything, k4-apex-dm-relabel re-sends "add" for every APEX module node that is not apex_dm_device, and ueventd labels it again with its /dev/block/mapper link (verified live: dm_device -> apex_dm_device). The same idempotent check runs again in the background at apexd.status=ready (queued behind late-init, so around zygote-start, not guaranteed before the PackageManager scan) and at sys.boot_completed=1 (same domain), for an "add" uevent ueventd handles after the first run; only the post-fs-data run is guaranteed to finish before zygote-start. Own SELinux domain k4apexdm: read the APEX list, stat dm nodes, write dm uevent files, log to kmsg.
